.TH BLUGON-LITE 1 "February 2026" "blugon-lite 1.0.0-lite" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
blugon-lite \- Blue Light Filter for X Window System

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blugon-lite
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-once\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR \fISECS\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-configdir\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-backend\fR \fIBACKEND\fR]

.PP
.B blugon-lite-tui

.SH DESCRIPTION
blugon-lite is a lightweight blue light filter for X Window System. It adjusts screen color temperature based on time of day, reducing blue light during evening hours to improve sleep quality.

.PP
This is a minimalist fork of blugon, optimized for:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Lower RAM consumption (< 8MB)
.IP \(bu 2
Reduced code complexity (~240 lines)
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive TUI for easy configuration
.IP \(bu 2
Automatic saving of changes
.RE

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B blugon-lite
Main CLI command for applying the filter.

.TP
.B blugon-lite-tui
Interactive Text User Interface for configuration.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-once
Apply gamma values for current time once and exit.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval [\fISECS\fR]
Set time between refreshes in seconds (default: 120).

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-configdir ", " \-\-config [\fIPATH\fR]
Specify configuration directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/blugon or ~/.config/blugon).

.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend [\fIBACKEND\fR]
Choose backend for communication with X. Available: scg, xgamma (default: scg).

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are read from ~/.config/blugon/

.TP
.B gamma
Gamma/temperature schedule file. Format: "hour minute temperature [label]"

.RS
.IP \(bu 2
hour: 0-23
.IP \(bu 2
minute: 0-59
.IP \(bu 2
temperature: 1000-20000 Kelvin
.IP \(bu 2
label: optional description (e.g., "Morning", "Night")
.RE

.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
8 0 6500 Morning
17 0 4500 Evening
21 0 3000 Night
0 0 2000 Deep Night
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B tui_config
TUI settings file. Contains selected theme preference.

.SH TUI USAGE
The TUI provides an interactive interface for managing schedules:

.TP
.B e
Edit selected schedule

.TP
.B a
Add new schedule

.TP
.B d
Delete selected schedule

.TP
.B t
Change color theme

.TP
.B s
Save configuration to file

.TP
.B q
Quit (asks confirmation if unsaved changes)

.TP
.B ↑ ↓
Navigate schedules

.TP
.B ← →
Adjust values (hour/minute/temperature)

.TP
.B Tab
Jump to action buttons

.TP
.B Enter
Confirm action

.TP
.B Esc
Cancel/Go back

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run as daemon (refresh every 2 minutes):
.B blugon-lite --interval 120

.TP
Apply once and exit:
.B blugon-lite --once

.TP
Use xgamma backend:
.B blugon-lite --once --backend xgamma

.TP
Open TUI:
.B blugon-lite-tui

.TP
Run daemon in background:
.B nohup blugon-lite --interval 120 > /tmp/blugon.log 2>&1 &

.SH TEMPERATURE GUIDE
Recommended temperature values:

.TP
.B 6500K
Normal daylight - Productivity

.TP
.B 4500K
Warm white - Afternoon transition

.TP
.B 3000K
Warm light - Evening, reduces melatonin suppression

.TP
.B 2000K
Very warm - Pre-sleep, minimal blue light

.SH PRESET CONFIGURATIONS
The package includes preset configurations:

.TP
.B evening
Standard evening schedule (17:00-08:00 night mode)

.TP
.B office
Office worker schedule (9:00-18:00)

.TP
.B student
Extended study hours

.TP
.B night-owl
Late night user schedule

.TP
.B minimal
Simple 3-point schedule (day, evening, night)

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/blugon/gamma
User's gamma schedule configuration

.TP
.I ~/.config/blugon/tui_config
TUI theme settings

.TP
.I /usr/share/blugon-lite/configs/
Preset configurations

.TP
.I /usr/lib/blugon-lite/scg
SCG backend binary (C + Xrandr)

.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B scg
Primary backend using Xrandr. More accurate, requires compiled C binary.

.TP
.B xgamma
Fallback backend using xorg-xgamma command. Less accurate but more compatible.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success

.TP
.B 1
Error (configuration not found, backend failed, etc.)

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B "Error: Invalid gamma line"
Configuration file has invalid format. Check hour/minute/temperature values.

.TP
.B "Error: Backend not found"
SCG binary not installed or not compiled. Try --backend xgamma.

.TP
.B "Error: Cannot open display"
X11 display not available. Make sure you're running in X session.

